// The prompt presets shipped with IncreArt (DESIGN.md, Prompt presets),
// embedded in the app and written to prompt-presets/default-presets.rsn
// beside config.rsn on every start (so edits to that copy are lost: put
// your own presets in the task folders next to it instead).
//
// Lazy Modify Style prompts read "Convert <image1> into <look>. Keep the
// composition, pose and identity unchanged." and have no {slot}. Styles that
// turn a flat image into 3D (Voxel, Animatronic) keep only the subject
// ("Keep the subject, pose and identity unchanged.") and have a negative
// prompt: kept to its composition, the model keeps the flat front view, and
// voxels seen face-on come out as 2D pixel art.
//
// Effortful Modify Style prompts read "Transform <image1> …. Keep the
// subject recognisable." and may change scene, scale and time; each has a
// {slot}, from a shared few ({material}, {element}, {objects}, {place},
// {backdrop}, {era}, {genre}, {topic}, {surface}, {colour}, {creature},
// {animal}, {plant}, {action}, {weather}, {mood}, {amount}, {flavour},
// {music}, …) so a sweep asks for few values; most have two or more, in
// different roles, varied between neighbours so a group's images differ. A tag
// has one job: {place} is where it happens, {backdrop} what's behind or
// blended in; {genre} a kind of story or world, {topic} what it's about or
// taken from. {action} is an -ing phrase read after "the subject"
// ("juggling flaming torches"). No {subject}: "the subject" is the image's.
// Effortful Modify Style — Text ones each have a tag for their words, quoted
// in the prompt, by the part they play: {title}, {slogan}, {name},
// {dialogue}, {sound} or {caption} ({text} for your own). The Text in a
// scene and Comics & manga ones add {place}, {era}, {action}, {element} or
// {genre}.
//
// A description loosely defines the name for someone who doesn't know the
// term, then says what you get. Artist, studio and brand names are left out.
